From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm8550: let the PCIe 1 GDSC collapse in suspend

0143 makes the PCIe 0 controller GDSC collapsible, which is all the
Retroid Pocket Nova needs: it only uses PCIe 0. The AYANEO Pockets also
run PCIe 1, for the Renesas uPD720201 USB 3 controller the gamepad sits
behind. With pcie_1_gdsc left at PWRSTS_RET_ON, gdsc_disable() keeps it
powered across system suspend, and the SoC never reaches its low power
states: HW 2026-11-14, Pocket ACE, 7.3.4, no pcie_ports=compat, both
links taken down for suspend (PCIe 1 retrained on resume), apps RSC
sleep set all zero, yet 0 s in aosd/cxsd/ddr over three suspends while
apss collapsed.

Same change as 0143 for the PCIe 1 controller GDSC: VOTABLE and
RETAIN_FF_ENABLE stay, the PHY GDSC is left alone.

[ Armada's 0566 and Kettle Linux's 40-kettle/1463 flip all four PCIe
  GDSCs; this is the second of those, as 0143 is the first. ]
---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8550.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8550.c
@@ -3025,7 +3025,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_1_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = VOTABLE | POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
 };
 
